      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seems to be related to https://github.com/bazelbuild/rules_go/issues/3178 and https://github.com/golang/go/issues/59924 ? Though this doesn\u0027t look like bazel is involved, just `go run`?\n\nThe error message is\n```\n/b/s/w/ir/go/go/src/crypto/internal/nistec/p256_asm.go:322:12: pattern p256_asm_table.bin: cannot embed irregular file p256_asm_table.bin\n```\n\nwhich implies that `p256_asm_table.bin` is a symlink, which would imply that every file here (including `p256_asm.go`) is also a symlink. It can also be seen that\n```\nGOROOT\u003d/b/s/w/ir/go/go\n```\n\nso it isn\u0027t clear why these are symlinks, since it looks like all of this is direct `go`? Perhaps these were present previously as symlinks and that is causing them not to be replaced with real files?",
      "revId": "a782bf1f348325bf7404819f1ea2f5aa427d21c3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
